      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Implementation**\n\nI'm solidifying the implementation plan, focusing on creating a `parse_json_secret.py` file in Python. I've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Secret Manager as the external provider. This should make it easy to identify the provider within the script.\n\n\n**Outlining the Structure**\n\nNow I'm designing the function within `parse_json_secret.py`. It will require `project_id` and `secret_id` for retrieval from Google Cloud Secret Manager. I've mapped the steps: create the client, build the secret's name, access the version, decode the payload, and parse it to JSON. The script will import `secretmanager` from `google.cloud` to use the client.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818833899,
          "start": 1789818831757
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b984038d001AYbkawV5L0Ikae",
