      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Secret Management**\n\nOkay, I'm setting up a `fetch_db_secret.py` script. The goal is to dynamically retrieve database connection secrets. I've decided to utilize AWS Secrets Manager as the external provider. This approach seems straightforward and readily identifiable within the code.\n\n\n**Implementing Secret Retrieval**\n\nI'm now focused on the code itself for `fetch_db_secret.py`. It's going to use `boto3` to talk to AWS Secrets Manager. The script will define a function that fetches a secret given its name. I'll make sure to explicitly showcase how `boto3` and `secretsmanager` are used, keeping it clean and easy to follow. This approach seems the most direct.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818829835,
          "start": 1789818827410
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b983f292001R5Um8peYSBG2DX",
